        card("Activity 5: the six parts and their meaning (the book’s key)", "", tables=[table(["No.", "Phrase", "Meaning"], _K5, say=[])]),
        card("Activity 5: the gist (the book’s key)", "This passage is about the benefits of exercising in the morning. It helps sharpen mental ability, adjusts our sleep to a natural cycle, and helps in getting ready for the day’s activities. One should also choose carefully what one eats, avoid non-nutritious food, and always think of what is good for the health."),
        card("Activity 6a: healthy cooking tips, first part", "Read the passage and give the gist in three to five sentences. Source: philstar.com. The book’s “cooking/eating/working out” is separated with commas. The book’s key: Tips for a healthier lifestyle include: take carbs in the morning, then work out up to lunch. Minimize carbs in the evening and just eat proteins. Measure ingredients, like only one tablespoon of mayonnaise, but vegetables should be unlimited. They are full of vitamins and minerals.", examples=passage(_A6A)),
        card("Activity 6b: healthy cooking tips, second part", "Summarize in four to five sentences. The book prints “2 liters”; here it is “dalawang litro.” The book’s key: Mangoes and bananas have higher carbohydrate content so just eat these fruits in the morning. Instead of salt or flavoring, try pepper and lemon juice. To get slimmer, use more pepper, chili powder and cayenne pepper. Drink two liters of cold water every day because the body will warm this water. Good effects are fast metabolism, one gets full easily, and eats less.", examples=passage(_A6B)),
        card("Activity 7: the importance of vegetables (the book’s scripts)", "Listen to passages about the importance of vegetables. (a) Write the gist in English. (b) Write a question for each passage in English. (c) On your teacher’s cue, take turns asking your question in Tagalog and answering a classmate’s in Tagalog using your notes (pair work, left out). The book’s “…” is a comma here; the figures ½ and 1½ are in words.", examples=dlg(_L7)),
        card("Activity 7: the book’s gists", "", tables=[table(["No.", "Gist"], [list(r) for r in _K7], say=[])]),
